.TITLE "security"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages keychains, certificates, and code signing. It provides a command-line interface to the macOS __Security framework__ and allows for the manipulation of sensitive credentials.

.DIV "TLDR"
**security find-generic-password -s "Name"**
Searches for and displays a generic password entry in the keychain.
> __find-generic-password__ search command | __-s__ service name flag | __"Name"__ the service identifier

**security unlock-keychain**
Unlocks the login keychain so that applications and scripts can access stored items.
> __unlock-keychain__ unlock command

**security list-keychains**
Displays all available keychain files currently in the search list.
> __list-keychains__ list command

**security add-trusted-cert -d -r trustRoot -k login.keychain cert.crt**
Adds a certificate file to the keychain and marks it as trusted.
> __add-trusted-cert__ add command | __-d__ admin flag | __cert.crt__ certificate file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Use the __security__ command with extreme caution. Automated scripts that use __unlock-keychain__ should be carefully protected to avoid exposing user credentials.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/security.html__
